# Every text file is stored and checked out with Unix line endings, on every
# system and whatever Git's own settings are. Without this, a copy made on
# Windows (a clone, a download, git archive) has Windows endings in every
# file, and an edit that matches several lines at once fails on it.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Windows batch files keep their Windows line endings on every system:
# stored exactly as they are, never converted.
*.cmd -text

*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.ico binary
